WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.190
Film Courage: Dan we know you love sports.

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:07.569
Let’s say you had five minutes to sit down
with a filmmaker before they make their short

00:00:07.569 --> 00:00:09.310
film, you are their coach.

00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:11.220
What are you going to coach them on?

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.730
They haven’t made it yet.

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:14.620
Maybe they’re ready to go.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:15.620
They have a script.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:18.340
Daniel Sol, CoFounder of The Hollyshorts Film
Festival: I think the biggest thing is going

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:24.589
back to belief in the story you’re trying
to tell.

00:00:24.589 --> 00:00:30.909
And I say that in the sense of anything you
do whether you play sports, the festival.

00:00:30.909 --> 00:00:35.320
Say you’re a basketball coach and you don’t
love basketball.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:37.550
How are you going to put the passion and energy
into succeeding.

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:38.550
You can’t.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.059
You will loose.

00:00:40.059 --> 00:00:41.059
You will fail.

00:00:41.059 --> 00:00:44.420
It’s the same with a story or a film.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:46.239
You want to get together with different people.

00:00:46.239 --> 00:00:50.059
You have to rally up grips and DPs.

00:00:50.059 --> 00:00:54.000
Their crew, PA’s, assistants to help you
and follow you in any way that you need.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.699
Actors that are going to say that I’m going
to emotionally give to you and I’m not ready

00:00:56.699 --> 00:00:59.770
to do this because you don’t seem that interested
or invested in this because you don’t believe

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:02.480
in the story or even know anything about the
story.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:05.070
That’s why I go back to what I said earlier.

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:07.080
You have to tell the story you know.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.600
Tell the story that you know that you can
make.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:13.990
Don’t try to do something that is not familiar
to you just because “Daniel said this is

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:15.280
what you have to do to get in festivals.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:16.280
You make it this way.”

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:19.890
Or some festival programmer said…yes but
your film has to be great (inherently good)

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:20.890
anyway.

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:23.250
It doesn’t matter genre or style or whatever.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.010
It has to just be good.

00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:28.140
And a good film comes from someone who believes
in their story and is passionate about their

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:29.220
story they make.

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:33.040
Any film that has won our festival or won
awards, they are not films that were made

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:34.570
with just blasé effort.

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:36.420
It’s just not happening.

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:42.040
These films were dedication, hours spent,
money lost, and a belief in the story.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:44.500
Understanding the story they are trying to
tell because they have a grasp on it.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:46.250
They are really passionate about what they
wrote.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:49.500
Many times the filmmakers in the short space
are…a lot of times.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:50.549
Not every time (of course not).

00:01:50.549 --> 00:01:55.539
A lot of times it’s a writer/director that’s
the same person, right?

00:01:55.539 --> 00:01:57.440
So if you wrote the script you should know
the material well.

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:00.039
If you didn’t write it then you believe
in it strongly.

00:02:00.039 --> 00:02:02.890
You say “Hey I want to team up and make
this film and I can direct it.

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:04.549
You are writing, I can direct your story.”

00:02:04.549 --> 00:02:06.870
But you have to have that passion and belief.

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:09.990
Because if you don’t have that you are just
going to fail.

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:10.990
The film won’t be good.

00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:12.349
There will be areas will it will falter.

00:02:12.349 --> 00:02:16.710
A lot of people will know that you are not
someone to follow because if you are directing

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:19.390
a group of people the same way you are managing
someone or coaching.

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:26.379
If you are talking to the players and they
know you are talking out of your behind and

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:27.622
you don’t believe what you are saying.

00:02:27.622 --> 00:02:29.180
And you’re giving a half-hearted effort,
they know it, they sense it.

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:32.180
They are not going to fight for you, they
are not going to care.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:35.920
Same way as with crew, actors, if you want
someone to give you their all as an actor

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:40.239
(especially with the actors), they are passionate,
they try to give themselves to you.

00:02:40.239 --> 00:02:44.070
Whether it’s emotional stuff, whether it’s
a breakdown scene, or it’s a fight scene

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:45.070
or a couple arguing.

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:47.240
And they are having real issues, they are
a married couple.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:50.040
Two actors, they are not married, they are
two actors.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:53.300
You have to believe that they are a married
couple and they’re fighting.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:55.400
You’ve got to get it out of them.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.659
And how do you do that if they don’t like
you at all?

00:02:57.659 --> 00:02:59.250
Or they don’t believe what you’re trying
to do?

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:02.100
Or how you’re trying to direct them and
the story you are trying to tell.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:03.269
Or it’s how you operate.

00:03:03.269 --> 00:03:09.269
Like if you don’t feel your belief and passion
for what the story is being made then they

00:03:09.269 --> 00:03:13.030
are going to give a half-hearted effort and
it’s not going to be good.

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:15.610
Or they are going to want to get out of there
and knock the lines out and go home, like

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:16.660
you’re done with these people.

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:17.660
They don’t care.

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:21.720
This is not for me or this is not good enough
for me, whatever (and just get it over with).

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:26.049
I think that’s a big thing and it sounds
simple and obvious but it’s not always the

00:03:26.049 --> 00:03:27.049
case.

00:03:27.049 --> 00:03:30.439
A lot of people in life do a lot of things
half-hearted or don’t believe in what they

00:03:30.439 --> 00:03:34.629
are doing…or think they do but don’t…or
in this case when it comes to storytelling

00:03:34.629 --> 00:03:38.269
maybe they just want to try to impress and
just make a story that is not their own or

00:03:38.269 --> 00:03:40.519
is something that they don’t believe in
because they don’t know the material well

00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:44.540
enough or they don’t understand the nature
of what they are trying to tell with the story.

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:51.220
It will probably end up showing whether it’s
a writing flaw or going back to the analogy

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:55.200
of sports, what if it’s a basketball story
and it makes no sense in terms of the basketball

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.200
setting.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:58.900
The writer doesn’t understand basketball,
doesn’t like basketball.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:03.320
It’s going to show that they don’t know
what the heck they’re talking about.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:05.020
The story won’t make sense.

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:09.350
As a viewer watching the movie you are watching
a scene of a basketball game and the score

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:12.861
makes no sense and it’s not really making
any sense as to what an actual sporting event

00:04:12.861 --> 00:04:15.230
would be like then it wouldn’t make sense.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:19.040
Then it’s like this is stupid, this is a
bad movie and you don’t even understand

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:20.760
the story that they are trying to tell, they
don’t even know the sport.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:24.430
If you’re using analogies for baseball or
basketball, things like that.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:28.360
Keeping it in the sports realm.

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:34.540
So yes, really knowing and loving what you
are trying to do with the project first and

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:35.590
foremost is critical.

00:04:35.590 --> 00:04:36.850
It’s just a must.

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:38.080
And you will see it reflect.

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:40.090
I go back to the winners [for the Hollyshorts
Film Festival] because if you are winning

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:43.360
the festival (our festival or others) being
nominated for Oscars, those films aren’t

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:47.920
made with a lack of passion or effort or belief
in the story.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:54.780
None of those filmmakers who have made those
stories have gone that far on just some casual

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:56.810
whim “Let’s just make this thing in one
day.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:05:00.530
We’ll just knock it out and just cram and
who cares about details.”

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:01.670
It’s not that.

00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:05.250
It’s made with passion, time, dedication
and effort.

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:06.250
All of those things.

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:08.660
Not to mention talent and all of those things.

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:10.669
You have to have that so that’s I think
the biggest thing.

